# Reference tests compare rendered pixels byte for byte across Linux, macOS,
# and Windows against one shared baseline set (ADR-0005). That only means
# anything if every platform checks out the same bytes, so nothing here is left
# to the local `core.autocrlf`.

# Text files keep LF in the working tree on every platform. A fixture checked
# out with CRLF is a different document: it is longer, which shifts the
# `<meta charset>` prescan window, and its line breaks reach the segmenter.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Baselines are compared byte for byte and must never be touched.
*.png binary

# Fonts are hashed and embedded (ADR-0008, ADR-0010).
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Deliberately not UTF-8: this fixture exists to prove a windows-1252 page
# renders, so git must leave its bytes exactly as they are.
tests/ref/fixtures/legacy-encoding.html binary
